00:30:25,270 --> 00:30:30,690
And see, whatever women are going for divorce, first do it on the gold side.

471
00:30:30,770 --> 00:30:33,270
Because first of all, the next ones eat gold.

472
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:36,620
And then there are people who say that they won't sign the contract and just give the gold.

473
00:30:36,700 --> 00:30:37,685
Like last week,

474
00:30:37,765 --> 00:30:44,805
there was an email that said that they won't let the truck go out of the colony,

475
00:30:44,885 --> 00:30:46,660
they will give the money.

476
00:30:47,250 --> 00:30:52,631
So yeah, first collect the finances, collect the gold, that there is a wedding,

477
00:30:52,711 --> 00:30:57,260
so I will go from my mother's side, so I will get ready and go from there.

478
00:30:57,340 --> 00:30:59,800
Like this, whatever, whatever.

479
00:31:02,320 --> 00:31:06,240
Tell your brother-in-law to get a DNA test done on your children.

480
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:09,240
Are they your children or are they your brothers?

481
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:18,240
Thirdly, if you have confronted someone in the house, how will you live in that house?

482
00:31:18,320 --> 00:31:20,240
You will see that sister-in-law every day.

483
00:31:20,320 --> 00:31:25,240
Even if they apologize and both side with each other, they will not side.

484
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:29,300
One thing that is going on is that…

485
00:31:29,750 --> 00:31:34,050
You can't neglect it. When you sit down and eat together, your feelings will awaken.

486
00:31:34,130 --> 00:31:36,050
Today or tomorrow, or the day after tomorrow.

487
00:31:36,130 --> 00:31:41,050
Because, of course, you can't do anything about your feelings.

488
00:31:41,130 --> 00:31:43,550
So, it's not right to live in that house.

489
00:31:43,630 --> 00:31:49,050
Either if you want to save this marriage and if you don't want to, if you want to reconciliate,

490
00:31:49,130 --> 00:31:52,050
then you can directly gather evidence and make your husband sit and say, this is it.

491
00:31:52,130 --> 00:31:57,130
Now either go to a different house and cut off all ties with them, or I'm leaving.

492
00:31:57,240 --> 00:32:01,240
But you should have the evidence.

493
00:32:01,320 --> 00:32:04,990
This is not a verbal excuse. It will come to you later.

494
00:32:05,070 --> 00:32:07,070
how bad an accusation you are making.

495
00:32:09,120 --> 00:32:15,040
If you have seen him going to the hotel, if you can make a video, or if he goes to the same hotel again and again.

496
00:32:15,120 --> 00:32:20,192
He didn't stand for three hours on the road, that's a big thing in an area like Pakistan,

497
00:32:20,272 --> 00:32:21,678
I mean in a city like Karachi.

498
00:32:21,758 --> 00:32:22,930
If at all it was Karachi.

499
00:32:23,500 --> 00:32:24,638
Anyway, it's disgusting.

500
00:32:24,718 --> 00:32:29,263
Now whoever doesn't care about his brother's respect, what will he do with your respect?

501
00:32:29,343 --> 00:32:31,589
What will he do with anyone else's?

502
00:32:31,669 --> 00:32:36,030
Because you are an outsider, sister-in-law is also an outsider, brother is brother.

503
00:32:36,110 --> 00:32:41,127
So when he is not upholding her honor and is so low in his status that,

504
00:32:41,207 --> 00:32:43,188
sister in law is a mother's honor.

505
00:32:43,268 --> 00:32:48,793
Sister in law should be seen from the mother's point of view.

506
00:32:48,873 --> 00:32:54,398
If she is older, if she is younger, then from the point of view of the sister.

507
00:32:54,478 --> 00:32:56,714
But it is a very sacred relationship.

508
00:32:56,794 --> 00:33:01,174
She is your brother's wife, she is your honor.

509
00:33:01,254 --> 00:33:03,090
That is how much you have to protect.

510
00:33:03,170 --> 00:33:09,170
Anyways, so if this is the case, he clearly doesn't respect you either.

511
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:11,759
He will cry and fall at your feet and apologize.

512
00:33:11,839 --> 00:33:16,954
But then again, when there is so much potential in the next one, that he can go so low,

513
00:33:17,034 --> 00:33:18,090
then he will go again.

514
00:33:18,170 --> 00:33:23,742
It is very rare that people are completely repenting.

515
00:33:23,822 --> 00:33:26,056
But I really don't know.

516
00:33:26,136 --> 00:33:31,110
I don't even understand your personal dynamics.

517
00:33:31,190 --> 00:33:33,990
I don't even know how financially independent you are.

518
00:33:34,610 --> 00:33:40,990
Now, just because you are getting four meals a day, you are humiliated all your life, I will not say that.

519
00:33:41,870 --> 00:33:46,190
But you need to cover your base first before you take any action.

520
00:33:46,410 --> 00:33:49,610
Like I said, it's a very low-key thing.

521
00:33:50,270 --> 00:33:55,250
And, but yeah, if you can prepare for the side, then you can do it.

522
00:33:56,150 --> 00:33:57,620
Rest.

523
00:33:57,920 --> 00:33:59,840
I can't say anything more.

524
00:33:59,920 --> 00:34:00,640
We should remove this from our minds.

525
00:34:00,720 --> 00:34:07,040
And if some people are thinking that this can't happen, this is wrong.

526
00:34:07,120 --> 00:34:10,040
It is very common practice.

527
00:34:10,120 --> 00:34:19,669
And to the point that it happens that where the son in law or mother in law or the world is sick,

528
00:34:19,749 --> 00:34:22,520
a lot of things happen.

529
00:34:25,310 --> 00:34:26,594
We live in a pure land.

530
00:34:26,674 --> 00:34:28,394
You should keep this in mind.

531
00:34:28,474 --> 00:34:31,127
Everything happens here.

532
00:34:31,207 --> 00:34:32,630
Everything is happening.

533
00:34:32,710 --> 00:34:35,063
So I would say, collect the proofs.

534
00:34:35,143 --> 00:34:39,256
If you stand there with an empty mouth, it will come on you.

535
00:34:39,336 --> 00:34:43,180
And it is the easiest thing to ruin a woman's character.

536
00:34:44,120 --> 00:34:47,314
So if it's backed up by proofs, then it will happen to you.

537
00:34:47,394 --> 00:34:49,126
And you should consult a lawyer.

538
00:34:49,206 --> 00:34:50,884
Ask them what they have to say.

539
00:34:50,964 --> 00:34:52,780
They will give you better advice.

540
00:34:52,860 --> 00:34:55,466
If you ask me domestically,

541
00:34:55,546 --> 00:34:55,846
I don't think a well-educated and respectable person can live in a place where such things are happening.

542
00:34:55,926 --> 00:35:06,580
We have to see the face of the person.

543
00:35:06,660 --> 00:35:09,731
You didn't mention that you have children or not.

544
00:35:09,811 --> 00:35:15,163
If you don't have children, then it's a good thing because if you have children,

545
00:35:15,243 --> 00:35:17,660
then you have a lifelong relationship.

546
00:35:20,660 --> 00:35:21,580
If not, then it's good.

547
00:35:21,660 --> 00:35:26,580
And yeah, consult a lawyer.

548
00:35:26,660 --> 00:35:31,580
Alright, next one. I've got like 20 plus emails about Durandar.

549
00:35:31,660 --> 00:35:38,580
So I compiled all of them and I'll answer only one.

550
00:35:38,660 --> 00:35:45,580
Durandar Lyari and The Uncomfortable Truth About Why We Are Decades Behind In Filmmaking.

551
00:35:45,660 --> 00:35:47,140
Salam Junaid. The reason I'm-

552
00:35:47,220 --> 00:35:52,440
Reason I am writing to you is every single day I am surrounded by Indian friends, housemates, and colleagues.

553
00:35:52,520 --> 00:35:58,940
We go for Diljit's concerts together. We cry over failed dates and terrible men.

554
00:35:59,020 --> 00:36:02,826
We share dal-chawal in the same crammed kitchen.

555
00:36:02,906 --> 00:36:07,640
And we celebrate Diwali and Eid like one messy little family.

556
00:36:07,720 --> 00:36:13,820
Whatever the political drama between our countries might be, there is almost no jingoism in our small desi world.

557
00:36:14,640 --> 00:36:18,280
It is all shared nostalgia, the same songs from childhood,

558
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:21,600
and the same rent stress that unites us.

559
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:23,600
Rent stress, okay.

560
00:36:23,680 --> 00:36:28,400
So when my Indian gang told me, ye toh saal ki sabse awaited film hai, tu chal rahi hai kya?

561
00:36:28,480 --> 00:36:30,960
They practically dragged me for dhurandhar.

562
00:36:31,040 --> 00:36:37,360
They convinced me it was about Karachi and an espionage mission, and that was more than enough reason for me to say yes.

563
00:36:37,440 --> 00:36:41,430
Writing to you now because something hit me like a brick on the way home from the cinema.

564
00:36:41,510 --> 00:36:43,540
I had just watched a three-hour,

565
00:36:43,620 --> 00:36:48,330
thirty-four-minute monster of a film without checking my phone even once.

566
00:36:48,490 --> 00:36:52,530
That alone should tell you how tightly Durandar grips its audience.

567
00:36:52,610 --> 00:36:54,631
It's definitely a massive film,

568
00:36:54,711 --> 00:37:04,680
and for a film this long to feel purposeful and strangely addictive says more about their craft than anything we have produced in decades.

569
00:37:04,870 --> 00:37:07,910
But more than the craft, Durandar forced me to face the truth.

570
00:37:08,090 --> 00:37:14,670
We keep sidestepping. Pakistan is not behind because we lack stories. We are behind because we refuse to tell them.

571
00:37:14,750 --> 00:37:16,054
And on top of that,

572
00:37:16,134 --> 00:37:24,310
it is almost ironic that our so-called rival held up a mirror to Karachi's forgotten history better than we ever have.

573
00:37:24,390 --> 00:37:28,510
Let me start the thing that completely floored me.

574
00:37:28,590 --> 00:37:33,430
Akshay Khanna, Junaid, this man did not act. He consumed the screen.

575
00:37:33,510 --> 00:37:35,750
Every twitch, every half smile.

576
00:37:35,830 --> 00:37:41,390
Every slow pause carried a madness that pulled the audience in like gravity.

577
00:37:41,470 --> 00:37:46,350
The people around me reacted to his presence the way you react to a storm you cannot

578
00:37:46,430 --> 00:37:47,750
look away from.

579
00:37:47,830 --> 00:37:51,950
He was not a side character, he was the real main character, the chaotic heartbeat

580
00:37:52,030 --> 00:37:53,670
of the entire film.

581
00:37:53,750 --> 00:37:58,590
And the disturbing part is this, characters like the one he plays were real.

582
00:37:58,670 --> 00:38:03,410
Karachi and especially Lyari had men who were wild, volatile and terrifying.

583
00:38:03,490 --> 00:38:03,790
yet charismatic enough to become legends whispered in back alleys. We grew up hearing

584
00:38:03,870 --> 00:38:09,650
cinematic our own city truly is and how badly we have neglected that potential.

585
00:38:09,730 --> 00:38:13,799
these names without ever really knowing their stories. It took an Indian film to remind me how

586
00:38:13,879 --> 00:38:19,414
Here is where the difference becomes structural.

587
00:38:19,494 --> 00:38:26,885
In India, the director is celebrated like a main event.

588
00:38:26,965 --> 00:38:31,290
Even with all the star worship, where

589
00:38:31,370 --> 00:38:38,010
when someone like SS Rajamouli who made Bahubali and RRR delivers something massive,

590
00:38:38,090 --> 00:38:44,730
or when Sanjay Leela Bhansali attempts movies like Bajirao Mastani and TV series like Heera Mandi,

591
00:38:44,810 --> 00:38:50,730
the audience treats him as the backbone of the film. People clapped when his name appeared.

592
00:38:50,810 --> 00:38:57,850
Every discussion around Durandar was shaped as Aditya Dhar's vision and Aditya Dhar's world.

593
00:38:57,940 --> 00:39:01,968
Now think of us, Maula Jatt is our biggest and most successful film.

594
00:39:02,048 --> 00:39:06,711
Yet half the people praising it cannot name the director, Bilal Ashari.

595
00:39:06,791 --> 00:39:12,794
The hype never translated into a conversation about the film making and his style or his next project.

596
00:39:12,874 --> 00:39:15,380
There is no long-term legacy building,

597
00:39:15,460 --> 00:39:21,062
no stable ground where a director is encouraged to take risks and develop mastery.

598
00:39:21,142 --> 00:39:23,530
Everything resets after each project.

599
00:39:23,610 --> 00:39:25,000
Then we come to the music.

600
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:31,059
We proudly claim that Pakistan is home of music in South Asia and emotionally that might be true,

601
00:39:31,139 --> 00:39:34,240
but sonically we have barely touched our own reserves.

602
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:37,694
Durandar's background score exposed this.

603
00:39:37,774 --> 00:39:46,221
The moment they used Baloch folk dance and dresses with Arabic EDM and Baloch beats during the Rehman Daked Balochistan sequence,

604
00:39:46,301 --> 00:39:49,063
I felt a strange mix of nostalgia and loss.

605
00:39:49,143 --> 00:39:51,290
That sound, the dance belonged to us.

606
00:39:51,370 --> 00:39:55,610
to us. We should have been the ones to rediscover it and carry it forward. Now watch what happens.

607
00:39:55,690 --> 00:39:56,190
Suddenly there will be a trend of Pashtun folk remixes and Baloch beats in India,

608
00:39:59,850 --> 00:40:00,730
just because an Indian film used them with more depth than we ever attempted.

609
00:40:06,170 --> 00:40:06,670
And then comes the most applausible part of the praise. They recreated Pakistan and Thailand,

610
00:40:12,730 --> 00:40:18,370
and I genuinely thought I was looking at Karachi. The dusty skylines and the stacked brick houses of the…

611
00:40:18,450 --> 00:40:23,079
of Lyari, the posters, the newspaper clippings, the ethnic colour palette.

612
00:40:23,159 --> 00:40:25,311
It was not surface-level curiosity.

613
00:40:25,391 --> 00:40:27,850
It was deep, careful study of our world.

614
00:40:27,930 --> 00:40:33,112
They understood the visual language of Sin better than many of our own productions.

615
00:40:33,192 --> 00:40:34,421
Now, I am not blind.

616
00:40:34,501 --> 00:40:35,977
The film is not perfect.

617
00:40:36,057 --> 00:40:42,818
There were obvious nods to the hyper-nationalistic to make the Indian audience feel good.

618
00:40:42,898 --> 00:40:45,031
A few typical jinguistic lines by R.

619
00:40:45,111 --> 00:40:45,790
Madhavan, who

620
00:40:45,870 --> 00:40:50,267
who plays the role of Ajit Dhawal, had the chest-thumping feel to them.

621
00:40:50,347 --> 00:40:52,571
But even with the high-cringe moments,

622
00:40:52,651 --> 00:40:56,478
I cannot pretend the craft was anything less than extraordinary.

623
00:40:56,558 --> 00:40:59,226
The screenplay has no wasted breath.

624
00:40:59,306 --> 00:41:02,600
The world-building for Part II is deliberate.

625
00:41:02,680 --> 00:41:04,495
The performances are committed.

626
00:41:04,575 --> 00:41:05,724
The sets are massive.

627
00:41:05,804 --> 00:41:07,385
The direction is confident.

628
00:41:07,465 --> 00:41:12,180
The violence is brutal and uncomfortable, but it felt necessary because Karachi

629
00:41:12,260 --> 00:41:18,420
Karachi did witness the savagery in the nineties and the early two thousands. I

630
00:41:18,500 --> 00:41:23,580
usually avoid violent films, but in this case the brutality felt honest. It needed

631
00:41:23,660 --> 00:41:28,740
to be shown that way. So here's the truth that stayed with me long after the film ended.

632
00:41:28,820 --> 00:41:33,192
Pakistan is decades behind in any sort of craft, not because we lack material,

633
00:41:33,272 --> 00:41:36,464
but because we lack courage, capital, creative continuity,

634
00:41:36,544 --> 00:41:39,110
and an ecosystem where a filmmaker can.

635
00:41:39,190 --> 00:41:41,502
claim their narrative the way India does.

636
00:41:41,582 --> 00:41:47,544
As you yourself say, West makes films with inaccuracies too, but at least they do it well.

637
00:41:47,624 --> 00:41:49,433
We have scars, we have legends,

638
00:41:49,513 --> 00:41:54,552
we have dance and music that can change the cinematic landscape of the entire region.

639
00:41:54,632 --> 00:41:59,052
We have cities whose streets deserve to be on the big screen.

640
00:41:59,132 --> 00:42:04,064
What we do not have is the confidence and the structure to trust our stories.

641
00:42:04,144 --> 00:42:06,030
Narendra reminded me of the first

642
00:42:06,110 --> 00:42:09,171
first time I watched gangs of Vasepur or Sacred Games,

643
00:42:09,251 --> 00:42:14,150
but this felt even more personal because the geography and the ghosts belonged to us.

644
00:42:14,230 --> 00:42:19,185
Karachi itself has materials which is gold mine for directors like Nolan and Scorsese.

645
00:42:19,265 --> 00:42:21,436
I genuinely hope you watch it.

646
00:42:21,516 --> 00:42:30,383
I want to know how you make sense of the strange ache that comes from watching someone else tell your story better than you ever dare to.

647
00:42:30,463 --> 00:42:31,560
Best wishes from Germany.

648
00:42:31,640 --> 00:42:36,320
So, interesting email around Durandar. Of course, it's well praised.

649
00:42:36,400 --> 00:42:40,508
And it was told how Karachi was recreated in Thailand.

650
00:42:40,588 --> 00:42:42,903
The colour palette was so accurate.

651
00:42:42,983 --> 00:42:45,090
The music, the beats, the Baloch.

652
00:42:47,250 --> 00:42:49,650
Music is going to make waves now.

653
00:42:49,730 --> 00:42:55,490
And these are our stories, our music, our reality, which is being portrayed by someone else.

654
00:42:55,570 --> 00:43:00,482
And I always say this, that when you don't make it, you don't claim your stories,

655
00:43:00,562 --> 00:43:03,570
then someone else will claim it according to their own.

656
00:43:03,650 --> 00:43:06,370
Now, obviously, there were a lot of inaccuracies in that.

657
00:43:06,450 --> 00:43:10,370
Like, nobody wears, see Rehman Daked was a Baloch.

658
00:43:10,450 --> 00:43:14,690
People don't do the Lucknow style here. Okay?

659
00:43:15,000 --> 00:43:16,920
If they do, they should do this one.

660
00:43:17,000 --> 00:43:18,920
Yes, okay, this and this.

661
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:20,920
This style is a little Karachi.

662
00:43:21,000 --> 00:43:22,920
Okay.

663
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:26,920
Second, what was the second?

664
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:29,920
No one wears these half-sleeved shalwar kameez here.

665
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:32,920
The one Ranveer Singh was wearing.

666
00:43:33,000 --> 00:43:34,920
So it will be caught in that itself.

667
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:36,920
That there is no style here. Okay.

668
00:43:37,000 --> 00:43:39,920
I didn't pay much attention to the wardrobe.

669
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:42,850
Balochi Shalwar is there. Is Balochi Shalwar in it or not?

670
00:43:42,930 --> 00:43:44,850
Have you seen it?

671
00:43:44,930 --> 00:43:51,850
So, I'm sure there will be a lot of inaccuracies, but then it's a good move.

672
00:43:51,930 --> 00:44:00,850
And I was reading a post that 1.8 million or 18 million will be too much.

673
00:44:00,930 --> 00:44:04,850
It has had illegal downloads. Yes.

674
00:44:04,930 --> 00:44:10,760
1.8 million pirated downloads, becoming the most pirated Bollywood movie in 20 years.

675
00:44:10,840 --> 00:44:12,760
So obviously Pakistanis are watching with interest.

676
00:44:12,840 --> 00:44:15,260
And why not watch it? It's their country's story.

677
00:44:15,340 --> 00:44:17,260
So they would like to see how the next generation has shown it.

678
00:44:17,340 --> 00:44:19,760
And why don't movies make it here?

679
00:44:19,840 --> 00:44:22,760
See, the entire ecosystem is missing.

680
00:44:22,840 --> 00:44:28,246
Why would anyone dare to make a movie with a budget of, let's say, twenty, thirty crores,

681
00:44:28,326 --> 00:44:31,260
when the total cinema in the country is eighty crores?

682
00:44:31,340 --> 00:44:37,260
Okay. Then, see, the biggest issue is that we don't have freedom.

683
00:44:37,340 --> 00:44:38,650
There is no freedom to express.

684
00:44:38,730 --> 00:44:45,550
No, you can show love and affection, like I won't go to Punjab, or you can make a gullible comedy type, that will work.

685
00:44:45,630 --> 00:44:50,410
These kinds of stories are too controversial.

686
00:44:50,490 --> 00:44:53,670
You are not allowed to tell such stories here.

687
00:44:53,750 --> 00:44:57,870
And I made a detailed Instagram story about it.

688
00:44:57,950 --> 00:45:00,870
That if you try to make it here, then whose version will you make?

689
00:45:00,950 --> 00:45:06,590
And the situation is so volatile that if you show its version, then the next party.

690
00:45:06,840 --> 00:45:07,960
She won't leave you.

691
00:45:08,040 --> 00:45:09,960
Something can still happen.

692
00:45:10,040 --> 00:45:11,960
There are murders here.

693
00:45:12,040 --> 00:45:13,960
So whose version will you show?

694
00:45:14,040 --> 00:45:15,960
Police's? Rangers?

695
00:45:16,040 --> 00:45:18,960
Rehman Daked? The people of Lyari?

696
00:45:19,040 --> 00:45:19,960
Whose version will you show?

697
00:45:20,040 --> 00:45:22,960
Or the gangs that are further from the gangs?

698
00:45:23,040 --> 00:45:24,960
You know, Arshad Pappu's?

699
00:45:25,040 --> 00:45:26,960
